          sign(rn: authored_doc(id: "1-bics-design", done: true, content: "**bounded-input / cost-envelope scheduling — operator-signed design** *(2026-07-02 capture)* — unified design record: `InputEnvelope` (data ceiling) → `CostEnvelope` (symbolic Predicted cost at envelope) → scheduling (width/placement); Predicted authority / Measured falsifier; cost → scheduling never selection. P0 InputEnvelope landed; P1–P5 dispatch separately (no scheduler types in this capture).", path: "docs/plans/bounded-input-cost-envelope-scheduling.md"), s: signed(by: "operator", works: true, scope_equivalent: true, as_expected: true)),
          authored_doc(id: "2-ci-two-tier-placement", done: false, content: "**CI two-tier placement — the 5-second rule** — a check rides the PR path iff measured warm cost is well within 5s OR proportional to the diff; everything else is Gauntlet (main + 4h falsifier). Wetness is not the axis. Placement is a data axis on `CiSpec` rows (`PrTier | Gauntlet`), never per-site prose. Fail-closed admission: unmeasured/unclassified → Gauntlet.", path: "docs/plans/ci-two-tier-placement-redesign.md"),
          with_plan(rn: authored_wi(id: "2-test-decomposition-wcf", done: false, content: "**test decomposition W/C/F cut — shape follow-on to two-tier placement** — measured CI head: almost every expensive row is `SubstrateInputsOnly` (pure computation), not integration. Classify by cause: **W** wet/external (large honest; cadence+kill) · **C** corpus breadth (mechanism RED on fixtures per-PR; corpus grain on enrolled cadence) · **F** fixture-shaped but slow by defect (fix cost-shape — do not decompose; #7205 class). Placement owns *where*; this owns *shape* so Class C rows can clear the 5s PR bar. Attribute-before-decompose mandatory. Dark `long/` classified only at Gauntlet enrollment. **Accept:** every Class C worklist row Accept-green or reclassified with owner; Class F has a named cost-shape owner (not this lane); corpus grains enrolled (never orphaned).", intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeMedium, repo: "gunbc"), path: "docs/plans/test-decomposition-wcf-cut.md"),
          authored(id: "2-p3", done: false, content: "**resolve-cache default-on** — purity proven (616/616) but opt-in: whole-file JSON IO buffers ~11× the packed graph and OOMed the concurrent floor (#5789 reverted); gated on a streaming IO realization. The warm ~18% lever, downstream of incrementality."),
