            headline: "process output as a designed surface",
            brief: "The register thesis (quiet at arm's length; responsive up close; every response true) applied to logs: a progress line is a projection of a fact the process already has, never a hand-authored string with a hand-chosen level. Five operator-signed laws: (1) process→outcome, no orphan Begins — a watchdog converts quiet-past-budget into a typed line; (2) the heartbeat carries identity, not just vitals; (3) attention escalates by dwell time, recursively down the containment tree (T a measured data row); (4) quiet at arm's length — green collapses, red/refused expands fully, bounded; (5) every rendered number is a receipt fact.",
