      section_group(
        label: "3 · Work intake — dispatch from the roadmap, not ad hoc",
        nodes: [
          ticket_row(id: "ts-dispatch-elevate", done: true, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "roadmap-driven dispatch — machinery landed, go-live proven",
            brief: "gunbc serve on srv1 serves the live roadmap, and POST /dispatch/NODE_ID invokes belt_dispatch_node in-process. The belt observes fail-closed over tmux, reconciles the ready frontier, and spawns a worktree plus a tmux claude session carrying the filled dispatch brief, with typed refusals at every arm. Go-live was proven by execution on srv1: spawn, idempotent re-POST, and a bogus-id refusal, each independently read back.",
            displaced_cost: "clicking a ready row starts a real worker session; no human shells into srv1 to launch work",
            current_state: "live on srv1: spawned / already_live / node_not_found each collected live; deploy tail green post-#7086; 13 sized ready nodes served",
            first_slice: "(landed) belt A #6942 → belt B #6940 → single dispatch authority #6914 → go-live receipt #7096",
            red_control: "a bogus node id answers node_not_found live; the page witness holds a RED on the retired j.ok shape",
            out_of_scope: "Stop verb, GET /sessions, and re-dispatch after Stop (ts-dispatch-redispatch)",
            handback: "belt refusals the preflight cannot converge (tmux, claude, claude-auth for the service user)",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-22", note: "assessed: three gaps to go-live — tree freshness, one live end-to-end receipt, sized nodes" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "gap 2 closed by execution on srv1: spawn, already_live, and node_not_found collected live; claude workspace-trust converged by seeding the one worktree root (ancestor inheritance proven by execution)" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "gap 1 closed: first green deploy_dashboard_srv1 (#7091); srv1 tree == main, unit active, healthz ok. New gap found live: re-dispatch after Stop — filed as ts-dispatch-redispatch" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "claude dependency modeled (extdeps.llm.cli): trust-store facts + belt preflight with typed spawn_failed steps; refuse-with-instructions, never auto-seed" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "UI fork found live and fixed: the button read the retired belt-A ok/node shape while belt B answered status — ok-predicate now derived from belt_dispatch_ok_status_labels, witness-glued, RED on j.ok" },
            ],
            authored_on: "2026-07-22",
            last_verified_on: "2026-07-23",
          }),
          ticket_wi(id: "ts-dispatch-redispatch", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "re-dispatch after Stop is broken — the dispatch loop is one-shot per node",
            brief: "Two failure classes, both proven live on srv1. Debris: Stop leaves the worktree and `dispatch/<node_id>` branch behind, so the next POST is a typed spawn_failed at the git step. Session-id reuse: even after hand-cleaning, claude exits 1 because the deterministic per-node UUID collides with the archived transcript — one-shot at the claude layer too.",
            displaced_cost: "a stopped node becomes dispatchable again without a human cleaning worktrees and branches on srv1",
            current_state: "found live 2026-07-23; both classes reproduce by execution; no fix landed",
            first_slice: "teardown/spawn own the worktree+branch lifecycle observe-then-decide (the session_lease upsert shape); a worktree with uncommitted work REFUSES removal, never silently deletes",
            red_control: "re-POST after Stop must not answer spawn_failed; a worktree with uncommitted changes must refuse teardown",
            out_of_scope: "the sessions panel (PR-B P2a) — this row is only the re-dispatch loop",
            handback: "the resume-vs-fresh choice: `--resume <uuid>` continues the node's prior work (arguably the right semantic) vs a per-attempt UUID — operator picks; either way a typed observation arm, never a fabricated fresh-spawn",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "both failure classes reproduced live on srv1; dedup shown independent of UUID determinism (observe keys on the tmux session name)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "2026-07-23",
            last_verified_on: "2026-07-23",
          }, intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeSmall, repo: "gunbc"),
          authored(id: "ts-ui-model", done: false, content: "**UI modeling migration — kill the hand layer (string-JS, raw values, concat microcopy); unlock the component register; land /sandbox** (built on #7096's wire vocabulary). VERDICT (per ts-dispatch-verdict — the operator's review sets the actual status; this row presents the fields, MERGE IS NOT DONE): candidate **AcceptedWithResidue** — all five phases shipped green by execution, the three named residues below are the counted follow-on rows so the item STAYS OPEN. (1) product review: accomplishes the brief's P0–P5 and acceptance 1–6; nothing blocked — the residues are deliberate deferrals, not gaps. (2) modeling audit: adds the component concept, the scale token axis, and the wire-label + query authorities, all grounded (no anemic leaf minted). (3) planning update: the residues are the follow-ons. P0 MODEL: the component concept (`gunbc.design.component`) as a register sibling of the surface archetype — element × role/material × interaction STATES × wire-contract binding; DispatchButton (`gunbc.roadmap_component`) with states DERIVED from `belt_dispatch_all_status_labels` (a new authority grounded one-exemplar-per-variant in `belt_dispatch_status_label`), totality cross-checked both ways with a located RED; spacing/type/font + dimension token scales added (`gunbc.design.scale`). P1 STRING-JS→TSPROGRAM: `dispatch_client_program` is one modeled TsProgram (ok-predicate a ts_binop `||` chain over `belt_dispatch_ok_status_labels`), EMITTED as an external served asset referenced by <script src> (operator steer: inline is a hack) — the string `dispatch_client_js` + its scaffold row deleted; script census wall refuses inline hand-JS + rogue src (two REDs); #7096's j.ok RED preserved on the served asset. P2 TOKENS: every roadmap_style px/font routes through a scale var, proven visually-neutral by execution (resolving the tokens reproduces the pre-P2 CSS byte-for-byte), gated by an untokened-length census (mirror of unthemed-color) with a RED; existing register walls stay green. P3 PRESENTATION: reserved button min-width is a projection of the longest wire label (kills the layout jump), ok/refusal/requested chip materials paint the P0 state's role (BoundaryRole added to the archetype demand), located fields (step/detail) surface to a title attr not console-only. P4 SANDBOX: GET /sandbox renders the register at every depth + the component gallery (one static instance per wire label, totality RED) + one live instance per arm; POST /sandbox/echo?status=LABEL answers any wire arm with the production belt JSON (fail-closed 400 on unknown). P5 DISPOSITION: the dead belt-A roadmap node-http emit + its smuggled-exec dispatch route DELETED; the module survives only for the gunbhub static emit, stamped with an explicit dissolution row. LOCAL RECEIPT (gunbc serve, scratch port): GET / /roadmap /sandbox render 200; /assets/*.js 200 text/javascript; POST /sandbox/echo for all six arms returns the belt JSON (spawn_failed carries step+detail), bogus → 400. RESIDUE (named, within shipped phases — not un-shipped phases): P3 separators stay tokened per-child margins, the flex-container 'by construction' refactor deferred (it changes node-head title-wrap, unverifiable without a browser — §5); P2 length census scopes to roadmap_instance_rules, so `gunbc.site.moodboard.figure_rules` border/radius px is moodboard's own dimension-token lift (sibling of the color lift); P5 gunbhub's node_http emit remains, its belt-B migration the named follow-on. Instances of `ts-concat-class` (the dispatch string-JS) and the unconsumed-component/single-authority classes killed here. ANEMIA DISSOLUTION (D1-D5, operator + audit 2026-07-23, same PR; PURE RE-GROUNDING, emitted bytes and wire strings unchanged, each item with its receipt): D1 MediaType — the fused HttpContentType enum (media-type x charset flattened into variant NAMES) DELETED; extdeps.http.server models it as RFC 9110 section 8.3 says (top_level a closed RFC 6838 registry enum, subtype an upstream string, parameters a list, charset a cited IANA parameter row), and http_content_type_wire_label becomes media_type_wire_label serializing over the structure (five presets pinned byte-exact, perturbed-parameter and perturbed-subtype REDs; ApplicationOctetStream's charset-less form falls out of an empty parameter list). D2 typed HTTP status — belt_dispatch_status and serve_text_response re-grounded on HttpStatus, the bare Int surviving only at the ServeWireResponse wire seam; per-variant codes 200/200/404/409/503/502 pinned. D3 CssLength — new extdeps.languages.css.values (cited CSS Values and Units + Fonts 4) types ScaleToken.value as CssLength (magnitude and unit) or CssFontStack (a family list), and the value-encoded token NAME is derived from the magnitude by length_token (space-4 from px 4) so the name-vs-value fork is unwritable; dispatch_reserved_width migrates to css_ch. D4 exemplar roster — belt_dispatch_result_exemplars enrolled DeclaredFrontier in gunbc.roster_registry (reason plus dissolve_on), with a reconciliation witness pinning the exemplar-derived label set against the wire-contract and a missing-variant RED. D5 CSS grain — new extdeps.languages.css.properties (CssPropertyName over the register's emitted set, plus CustomProperty for author vars and a counted RawProperty escape) and .selectors (SelectorSubject = ClassSelector or ElementSelector or PseudoSuffix or a counted RawSelector frontier); material.CssDecl.prop and BuildRule subject re-grounded, every consumer migrated, stylesheet byte-identical. RESIDUE (counted, honest): RawSelector 18 (descendant/compound/functional-pseudo, awaiting the combinator grammar) and RawProperty 1 (accent-study code-spacing); the CSS VALUE grammar (decl right-hand sides), Content-Type forward-parse, and gunbhub's node_http belt-B migration stay named arcs. LOCAL RECEIPT (gunbc serve scratch port): GET / and GET /sandbox answer 200 text/html; charset=utf-8; POST /sandbox/echo?status=spawn_failed answers 200 application/json; charset=utf-8 carrying the belt shape with step and detail; POST /dispatch/bogus answers 404 application/json; charset=utf-8."),
          authored(id: "ts-intake-discipline", done: false, content: "**until the actuator lands, this sheet is the intake queue** — new work enters as a row here or as a sized lane node with an Accept line, never ad hoc mid-session; dispatch top-down by the numbering; a session that discovers work files a row instead of chasing it."),
          ticket_row(id: "ts-dispatch-lifecycle", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "each dispatched item is a real workflow, not a single hop",
            brief: "Stages: MODEL first (concept/authority delta + acceptance claims), BRIEF generated from row + model with the bar as checkable claims, IMPLEMENT, ANTAGONISTIC REVIEW against the brief — never the PR's self-description — LAND with the verdict updating this sheet. The wall: MERGE IS NOT DONE — a merge certifies the diff is safe; only a review verdict moves status. The MODEL stage is unskippable and first, to the ed25519 citation bar (every referenced upstream entity carries its own authority); a brief without the model stage's output is not dispatchable.",
            displaced_cost: "the #7087 pattern: worker hits gaps, does half, flags honestly, PR merges — and the item silently reads done; the absorbing fallback at the management layer",
            current_state: "the discipline row; group 3c (ts-wf-shape lane) is its machine",
            first_slice: "",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "the machine itself — typed stages and verdicts live on the 3c lane rows",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "operator ruling + same-day sharpening: model stage first and unskippable, DFS-associated to existing authorities, created holistically where nothing exists" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 1); fields decomposed from the prose, nothing added" },
            ],
            authored_on: "2026-07-23",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }),
          ticket_row(id: "ts-dispatch-verdict", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "typed review verdict is the only status authority",
            brief: "Every dispatched item closes with the operator's three questions as the verdict's fields: (1) antagonistic product review — did the PR accomplish what the brief asked; what remains, what blocked, what planning updates follow; (2) modeling audit — what models it adds, whether it should add more, anemia check; (3) planning update — the verdict lands on this sheet so the next session inherits it (sessions are goldfish; the sheet is the anchor). Vocabulary: Accepted | AcceptedWithResidue (residue becomes counted rows, item STAYS OPEN) | NeedsRework (return-to stage + located debts) | Abandoned (reason).",
            displaced_cost: "merged residue with no row; AcceptedWithResidue is the honest form of the half-done merge",
            current_state: "vocabulary in hand use on this sheet; the typed carrier rides ts-wf-stage-artifacts",
            first_slice: "",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "the Verdict carrier types (ts-wf-stage-artifacts)",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 1)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "2026-07-23",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }),
          ticket_row(id: "ts-dispatch-rework", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "rework is a first-class transition, designed against LLM defensiveness",
            brief: "Backing up from step 10 to step 2 must be cheap and expected, never a negotiation. Three mechanisms: (a) the BRIEF declares rework a normal outcome — expectation set at dispatch, not sprung at review; (b) a NeedsRework verdict dispatches a FRESH session carrying the original brief + the prior attempt's diff + the located debts — never ask the context that produced the work to unwind it (in-context sunk cost is the defensiveness mechanism; the goldfish property becomes the asset); (c) stage artifacts make backup a re-derivation — edit the model, regenerate downstream.",
            displaced_cost: "rework as negotiation; the producing context defending its own work",
            current_state: "priced up front as design; mechanism (b) enforces at ts-wf-belt-refusals, (c) at ts-wf-stage-artifacts",
            first_slice: "",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "the enforcing arms (ts-wf-belt-refusals, ts-wf-stage-artifacts)",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 1)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }),
        ],
